# Python Conventions

## Version
Python 3.14

## Formatter & Linter
Ruff for both formatting and linting. Line length: 88. Run `ruff check` and `ruff format` before committing.

## Type Hints
- Required on every function signature — parameters and return types
- Use `from __future__ import annotations` at the top of every file
- Prefer `X | None` over `Optional[X]`
- Prefer `list[X]`, `dict[K, V]` over `List[X]`, `Dict[K, V]`

## Async
- All I/O-bound functions must be `async`
- Use `httpx.AsyncClient` for HTTP calls — never `requests`
- Never call blocking I/O inside an async function

## Pydantic
- Pydantic v2 for all data models
- Parse external API responses into Pydantic models immediately
- Use `model_config = ConfigDict(...)` — not inner `class Config`

## Docstrings
- Required on every module, class, and function — no exceptions
- Google-style format
- Be detailed: explain what the function does, why it exists, and any non-obvious behavior
- Document all parameters, return values, and exceptions
- Write for a reader with basic Python knowledge — clarity over brevity

## Environment Variables
All config via Doppler. Access env vars through a central `config.py` — never `os.environ` directly outside of `config.py`.
